  "question": {
    "text": "The equation of state of a gas is given by $\\left(p+\\frac{a}{v^{3}}\\right)\\left(V-b^{2}\\right)=c T,$ where $p, V, T$ are pressure, volume and temperature respectively and $a, b, c$ are constants. The dimensions of $a$ and $b$ are respectively"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\left[\\mathrm{ML}^{8} \\mathrm{T}^{-2}\\right.$ and $\\left.\\mathrm{L}^{3 / 2}\\right]$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\left[\\mathrm{ML}^{5} \\mathrm{T}^{-2}\\right.$ and $\\left.\\mathrm{L}^{3}\\right]$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\left[\\mathrm{ML}^{5} \\mathrm{T}^{-2}\\right.$ and $\\left.\\mathrm{L}^{6}\\right]$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\left[\\mathrm{ML}^{6} \\mathrm{T}^{-2}\\right.$ and $\\left.\\mathrm{L}^{3 / 2}\\right]$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$[P]=\\left[\\frac{a}{V^{3}}\\right] \\Rightarrow\\left[M L^{-1} T^{-2}\\right]=\\frac{a}{\\left[L^{3}\\right]^{3}}$\r\n$\\begin{aligned} \\Rightarrow \\quad a &=\\left[M L^{8} T^{-2}\\right] \\\\ &[V]=\\left[b^{2}\\right] \\Rightarrow\\left[L^{3}\\right]=b^{2} \\Rightarrow b=\\left[L^{3 / 2}\\right] \\end{aligned}$"
  }
